<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caesarion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">47–<a href="/years/30-bce">30 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Ptolemy XV Caesarion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caesarion, formally Ptolemy XV, was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra VII</a> and, by her account, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. Born in 47 BCE, he reigned as co-ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> with his mother from 44 BCE. After the defeat of Antony and Cleopatra, Octavian had him put to death in 30 BCE, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic dynasty</a> came to an end.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caesarion.jpg" alt="Caesarion" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: carolemage (Flickr) · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caesarion_granite_head.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
